1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,127
FINMOZG Variance Detective.

2
00:00:02,127 --> 00:00:05,204
Track 02: the agent that can explain why.

3
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:11,196
A controller closes September and sees gross margin down almost 7 points.

4
00:00:11,196 --> 00:00:18,311
The reasons sit in four systems that share no keys: the ledger, purchasing, the order system, and the bank.

5
00:00:18,311 --> 00:00:24,129
Today that is one or two days of spreadsheets, and a booking error can look like a real cost.

6
00:00:24,946 --> 00:00:26,614
So we ask in plain English.

7
00:00:26,614 --> 00:00:33,441
What you see is a real live run, recorded and replayed here: a fictional company with synthetic data.

8
00:00:33,441 --> 00:00:39,968
Every query went through Zetaris, and every model call through the Meterless Runtime to NVIDIA Nemotron.

9
00:00:40,766 --> 00:00:46,280
The agents recall memory, map the Zetaris semantic layer, and plan hypotheses.

10
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:51,905
Investigators write SQL in parallel and repair it when Zetaris returns an error.

11
00:00:51,905 --> 00:00:54,730
Quant computes the exact margin bridge in code.

12
00:00:54,730 --> 00:01:03,660
The Skeptic holds the veto: it sends a claim back when the amount does not reconcile, when the bank does not confirm a cost, or when nobody is named.

13
00:01:04,458 --> 00:01:05,261
The result.

14
00:01:05,261 --> 00:01:09,816
Gross margin fell from 35.9 to 29.2%.

15
00:01:09,816 --> 00:01:14,335
Every line ties to the bridge, and the residual is shown openly.

16
00:01:14,335 --> 00:01:20,585
The ticks mean: agreed to source rows, confirmed in two systems, ties to the bridge.

17
00:01:21,382 --> 00:01:22,882
Open the biggest driver.

18
00:01:22,882 --> 00:01:29,601
Invoice MRP-88213 was booked twice in accounts payable, but the bank paid it once.

19
00:01:29,601 --> 00:01:31,944
Here are both queries and their rows.

20
00:01:31,944 --> 00:01:35,719
The supplier line names Sierra Nut, billing above contract.

21
00:01:35,719 --> 00:01:38,231
The mix line names Capital Wholesale.

22
00:01:39,026 --> 00:01:48,230
The Skeptic struck out two explanations: prices did not change, and marketing spend is an operating expense, so it cannot explain gross margin.

23
00:01:48,230 --> 00:01:51,536
Every figure in the memo cites its evidence.

24
00:01:52,350 --> 00:02:01,218
Zetaris is the only door to the data: 5 sources and a unified semantic layer, whose data-quality rule flags the duplicate on its own.

25
00:02:01,218 --> 00:02:08,225
Meterless gives the team a shared World Model, H-MEM memory, and Markovian review of long evidence.

26
00:02:09,034 --> 00:02:11,099
The controller confirms the finding.

27
00:02:11,099 --> 00:02:17,517
The next question starts warm: the schema map comes from memory and the confirmed duplicate is checked first.

28
00:02:17,517 --> 00:02:24,512
Running on Nemotron through Meterless, and scored against planted ground truth: 22 of 22 checks.
